    {
      "text": "You ever have that moment where you think the thought is right there, like on the tip of your tongue? But the harder you try to remember, the further it runs away. So I just stood there, staring, hoping the sentence would magically finish itself. My coworker tried to help, like, \"Were you talking about the email?\" And I'm like, \"No, I think it was something smarter than that.\" Eventually, I just laughed it off and changed the subject. Because honestly, what else can you do? 10 minutes later, I remembered exactly what I was going to say. But by then, it didn't matter anymore. I don't know why it's so embarrassing, but it is. I guess forgetting what you were saying is just your brain's way of telling you to slow down. Or maybe it's just taking a quick coffee break without warning you.",
